  "name": "Auto-assign GitHub PR reviewers based on changed files",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "4a6adac9-b4e2-4a88-83a5-6183d9de4e51",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 880,
        "content": "## Auto-assign GitHub PR reviewers based on changed files\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow receives GitHub pull request webhook events and decides whether the PR should be processed. For eligible PRs, it fetches the changed files from GitHub and the reviewer roster from Supabase, then matches file paths to likely owners. If reviewers are found, it assigns them on GitHub, notifies them in Slack, and updates their last-assigned timestamp; otherwise it records the no-reviewer path.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the GitHub PR webhook URL in the repository settings and ensure it sends pull request events to the n8n webhook node.\n- Set valid GitHub credentials or token access for reading pull request files and requesting reviewers on the target repository.\n- Configure the Set Configuration node values for github_token, repo_owner, repo_name, and max_reviewers.\n- Connect Supabase credentials and ensure the reviewer roster table contains file ownership or matching rules plus fields needed for assignment tracking.\n- Connect Slack credentials and verify the notification target and reviewer Slack identifiers are available.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the PR filtering condition, file-to-owner matching code, max reviewer count, Supabase roster schema, and Slack notification message to match the repository\u2019s review policy."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7010303a-2c2d-471b-ab21-99cce8c8417b",
